From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:14:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: aop: Add T8132

The T8132 (M4) AOP takes the T6040 boot arguments (EC0p 0x100_0000_0000,
nCal 1, alig 64, AOPt 0): iBoot leaves the boot-argument table at its
defaults in the AOP SRAM and the AOP halted, and the ADT gives __ETEXT the
DART address 0x100_0000_0000. The bootloader programs the AOP DART's DAPF
and reserves the firmware segments and the DAPF windows, so the T6040
configuration applies unchanged, including the firmware's own nCal of 1
that the T6040 writes since 28174f88b ("soc: apple: aop: Write the T6040
firmware's own nCal boot argument").

Tested on J713 (MacBook Air 13" M4) with m1n1 handing the AOP over (its
memory-region holds __ETEXT, __OS_LOG and the 15 DAPF windows): the AOP
starts, and the microphones capture (3 channels, 48 kHz) through
aop_audio.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
[eryk: rebased onto integration/aurora 21f7ffcf; the T8132 config now
 inherits nCal 1 from the T6040 one (28174f88b), so the message says so]
Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b2895d62d2594b201d5c0df48736b5dd8d84149b)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs
index 0f455a9530..49f91c0287 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs
@@ -2595,6 +2595,10 @@ const HW_CFG_T6040: AopHwConfig = AopHwConfig {
     fw_regions: true,
     halt_on_failed_start: true,
 };
+/// T8132 (J713): as T6040. The bootloader hands the AOP over the same way, with
+/// the DART's DAPF programmed and its windows reserved alongside the firmware
+/// segments.
+const HW_CFG_T8132: AopHwConfig = HW_CFG_T6040;
 /// T8140: the firmware is started with the boot arguments the bootloader
 /// left, boots through the setup port and speaks EPIC version 4. Of the
 /// advertised AFK endpoints, the application map is 0x20 misc, 0x21
@@ -2625,6 +2629,7 @@ kernel::of_device_table!(
         (of::DeviceId::new(c_str!("apple,t6020-aop")), &HW_CFG_T6020),
         (of::DeviceId::new(c_str!("apple,t8140-aop")), &HW_CFG_T8140),
         (of::DeviceId::new(c_str!("apple,t6041-aop")), &HW_CFG_T6040),
+        (of::DeviceId::new(c_str!("apple,t8132-aop")), &HW_CFG_T8132),
     ]
 );
 
